abstract: >-
  The Health-RI Metadata Model (v2.1.0) is an RDF-based
  specification for the National Health Data Catalogue. It draws on
  DCAT-AP NL and a draft of HealthDCAT-AP, with Health-RI-specific
  adaptations. The schema defines classes, properties, cardinalities, and
  controlled vocabularies for describing catalogues, datasets, data
  services, dataset series, distributions, and supporting entities.
  Definitions and usage notes help data holders and technical implementers
  apply the schema consistently. These common, machine-readable resource
  descriptions support interoperability and help make health and life
  sciences data in the Netherlands findable and reusable across
  institutions, in line with the FAIR principles.

